---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Rules & Terms — FlexAI.lol"
  description="FlexAI is a public pay-to-rank leaderboard for AI software, products, and founders. Rank is what you pay — nothing else."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-700 dark:text-gray-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      
      {/* Title */}
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Rules
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed font-normal">
          FlexAI is a public pay-to-rank leaderboard for AI software, tools, and founders. There are no ads, no API keys, and no revenue share. You pay to stand above everyone else. Rank is what you pay — nothing else.
        </p>
      </div>

      {/* How ranking works */}
      <section id="rules" class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dark-border/60">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          How ranking works
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            New listings are in whole Euros (€), €2 minimum, €999,999 maximum, €1 at a time. Ranks already on the board keep their amount until they raise or get outranked.
          </li>
          <li>
            Taking #1 costs at least the current #1 amount + €1 (or matches their required outbid). Paying less still puts you on the board at whatever rank that amount can take. Equal amounts stay in the order they were placed — the older listing keeps the higher rank.
          </li>
          <li>
            Already on the list? Enter the same URL or @handle again and raise your rank. The new amount must be at least €1 above your current staked bid; checkout only charges the difference. Someone else cannot take your rank by paying that difference.
          </li>
          <li>
            App Store, Play Store, GitHub, and similar platform links are keyed by their unique project path, so different apps don't share a rank. Tracking query strings are ignored.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* What you can list */}
      <section class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dark-border/60">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          What you can list
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            An AI product website, startup landing page, or an X @handle.
          </li>
          <li>
            Chat and invite links are not allowed — Telegram, WhatsApp, Discord, Messenger, Signal, and similar. The board is for AI software and verified profiles, not group chats.
          </li>
          <li>
            Links to sexual content or non-software scam networks are strictly prohibited. If it is adult/NSFW or malicious, it does not belong on the board and will be removed immediately.
          </li>
          <li>
            Query parameters are stripped from listing links. Affiliate, referral, and tracking URLs will not work.
          </li>
          <li>
            Link shortener URLs (e.g. bit.ly, tinyurl, t.co) are not allowed. If you submit one, it is replaced by the URL it redirects to.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* AI Verification & Categories */}
      <section class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dark-border/60">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          AI Verification & Categories
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            All submitted URLs are analyzed automatically by real-time scrapers to verify authentic AI software signals before checkout.
          </li>
          <li>
            Categories for existing listings were auto-assigned by AI. If your product is in the wrong category or was rejected by automated signals, DM <a href="https://x.com/ByManuuDB" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 font-semibold hover:underline">@ByManuuDB on X</a> to have it updated.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* After you pay */}
      <section id="terms" class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dark-border/60">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          After you pay
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2.5 text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          <li>
            Your listing is public immediately upon Stripe confirmation. Clicks go to the URL or profile you submitted, without query parameters.
          </li>
          <li>
            A completed payment is what claims the rank. All payments are final and non-refundable.
          </li>
          <li>
            Paying means you agree to these Rules, our Terms of Service, and Privacy Policy.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* Payment & Chargebacks Policy */}
      <section id="privacy" class="space-y-3 pt-4 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-dark-border/60">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          Payment & Chargebacks Policy
        </h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
          By completing this purchase, you confirm that you have reviewed the product and pricing and authorize the payment. If you have any issue with your purchase, please contact <a href="https://x.com/ByManuuDB" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400 font-semibold hover:underline">@ByManuuDB on X</a> before initiating a payment dispute or chargeback.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
